HarfRust 0.15.0 vs HarfBuzz (8.2.0 and 15.0.0 alike), see DEVIATIONS.md [text]:
1. scale.rs: HarfBuzz's roundf is floor(x + .5) (ties towards +inf); HarfRust
   used f32::round (ties away from zero), so scaled anchors at -n.5 were one
   unit lower.
2. fallback.rs: HarfBuzz computes fallback space widths from font->x_scale
   ((x_scale + n/2) / n); HarfRust divided upem and scaled the result.
Apply in the crate root with -p1.

